### The skein module of $S^3$ {#three sphere}

The skein module of $S^3$ is equal to $Z[A,A^{-1}]$. The reason is the following.

Given a planar diagram of a famed link $L$ in $S^3$, by applying the skein relation repeatedly to resolve the crossings and remove the unknots, $L$ can be reduced to the empty link multiplied by a Laurent polynomial of $A$. In this way, a polynomial is associated to each framed link in $S^3$.

